Managing Resource Groups:
Create Resource Group with that resource group's name.
New-AzResourceGroup -Name "MyResourceGroup" -Location "East US"

List all resource groups in tabular format.
Get-AzResourceGroup | Format-Table


Show detailed infomation on target resource group.
Get-AzResourceGroup -Name "MyResourceGroup"

Force deletion of a resource type in the target resource group
Remove-AzResourceGroup
-Name "MyResourceGroup"
-ForceDeletionType "Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines"
-Force

Working with Resource Group Deployments:
New-AzResourceGroupDeployment
-ResourceGroupName "MyResourceGroup"
-TemplateFile "azuredeploy.bicep"
-Parameter @{"storageAccountName" = "mystorageaccount"}

List all deployments on target resource group.
Get-AzResourceGroupDeployment -ResourceGroupName "MyResourceGroup"

Show detail information on specified deployment from target resource group.
Get-AzResourceGroupDeployment
-ResourceGroupName "MyResourceGroup"
-Name "MyDeployment"

Delete deployment record from target resource group, does not delete resources.
Remove-AzResourceGroupDeployment
-ResourceGroupName "MyResourceGroup"
-Name "MyDeployment"

Deployment Parameters: Mixed Methods:
Allows dynamic and static parameter values to coexist
Useful when some values require runtime computation or external input while others are fixed
Good for CI/CD pipelines where parameters are a mix of injected and hardcoded
New-AzResourceGroupDeployment
-ResourceGroupName "MyResourceGroup"
-TemplateFile "template. json"
-minTlsVersion $(Get-Content -Path c:\param.txt -Raw)
-tagsArray $tagsArrayParam

